WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
django-data-seed — zero-config Django database seeding

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:29.067
Install it, add "django_data_seed" to INSTALLED_APPS, then migrate. That's the whole setup.

3
00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:34.500
--dry-run previews the seed plan and pre-flight checks — writes nothing to the database.

4
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.600
--count sets how many rows to create per model.

5
00:00:41.600 --> 00:01:19.300
--seed 7 makes the run reproducible: run it, wipe the database, run the exact same command again — identical rows both times.

6
00:01:20.300 --> 00:02:00.233
--locale switches the realistic data to a region: US English, then UK English, on the same model.

7
00:02:01.233 --> 00:02:16.733
--strategy controls foreign keys: "reuse" points at existing parents, "create" builds a fresh one for every child.

8
00:02:17.733 --> 00:02:23.200
--exclude skips specific models or apps from the run.

9
00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:29.333
--format json gives machine-readable output — perfect for CI pipelines.

10
00:02:30.333 --> 00:02:45.533
The finale: seeding the entire project at once — 750 rows per model, 4,500 rows across 6 tables, bulk-inserted in well under a second.

11
00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:50.033
pip install django-data-seed — github.com/rohith-baggam/django-data-seed
